        "statement": "Let $\\Gamma\\subset\\mathbb C$ be a rank-two lattice acting on $\\mathbb H^3$ by horizontal translations, and let $$ C=\\{(x+iy,t):t\\ge1\\}/\\Gamma $$ be the quotient of the horoball $t\\ge1$. If $A$ is the Euclidean area of a fundamental parallelogram for $\\Gamma$, then the end is at infinite hyperbolic distance and $\\operatorname{Vol}(C)=A/2$.",
