        "dependency_level": 5,
        "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Choice. Let $K:S^1\\to S^3$ be a smooth oriented knot with a chosen product tubular neighbourhood $N(K)$, and set $E_K=S^3\\setminus\\operatorname{int}N(K)$ and $T_K=\\partial E_K$. If $K$ is not ambient isotopic through orientation-preserving diffeomorphisms to the standard unknot, then every smoothly embedded $2$-sphere in $\\operatorname{int}E_K$ bounds an embedded $3$-ball in $E_K$, and there is no smoothly embedded disk $D\\subset E_K$ whose interior misses $T_K$ and whose boundary is an essential simple closed curve in $T_K$.",
