        "statement": "For a smooth knot $K$ with chosen compact exterior $E_K$ and boundary torus $T_K$, a finite-volume hyperbolic knot exterior structure is a complete Riemannian metric of constant sectional curvature $-1$ on $\\operatorname{int}(E_K)$ with finite volume and exactly one cusp whose torus cross-section is isotopic in $\\operatorname{int}(E_K)$ to a parallel copy of $T_K$. The definition asserts no existence.",
